{"availability":"available","full":"thakurabhishek7283/tessera-workspace","name":"tessera-workspace","description":"Rich-text editor, sticky notes and an accessible kanban board as Web Components, offline-first with undo/redo.","category":"Productivity","language":"TypeScript","stars":0,"forks":0,"created":"2022-01-30T20:30:21Z","updated":"2026-10-10T01:36:15Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":"https://thakurabhishek7283.github.io/tessera-workspace/","topics":["accessibility","drag-and-drop","kanban","rich-text-editor","web-components"],"demo":"https://thakurabhishek7283.github.io/tessera-workspace/","color":"#193546","ink":"#a6d6e8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-10T03:21:20.457Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-10T03:21:20.457Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-10T03:21:20.457Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-07T23:32:28.240Z","stars":0,"forks":0},{"at":"2026-10-10T03:21:20.457Z","stars":0,"forks":0}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["A rich-text editor, sticky notes and a Kanban board as web components. Part of the Tessera kit family: switch a feature on with configuration, use it in any framework, keep the data in the browser or on your own backend.","Task boards, notes and rich text are in almost every collaborative app, and each one usually brings its own state handling, its own backend assumptions and its own framework wrapper. These kits sit on the small Tessera core instead. A drag, an edit or an undo goes through the same path whether the data lives in IndexedDB, in a REST service or in the tab next to yours, and a feature you do not enable never loads its code. The drag and drop works with a mouse, a finger and the keyboard, and the whole thing works offline."],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/thakurabhishek7283/tessera-workspace/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"2b71b494beeabf050ff06219f1de0b3dd33856dc9d44e016154cd58a077de08d","extractedAt":"2026-10-07T23:32:28.334Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-07T23:32:28.334Z",